# site.env.example -- the SITE file regen.sh requires (SITE=<a file outside this tree>). Data only; rule 24: no
# function is proved here. Every host location and workspace name of a run is set here and nowhere in the tree: one
# NAME=value per line, no quotes; a value the caller's environment already sets wins. regen.sh refuses a SITE that
# leaves one of these unset or sets a name not listed here. W (the lane), LT (its local scratch) and TR (the checkout
# that holds this tree) are set by regen.sh itself; the build VMs are named by the kit's env.sh template, not here.
#
# Read by regen.sh itself:
# the repository that holds the internal records ref (the kit and its run records)
RECORDS_REPO=<a clone holding the internal records ref>
# the internal records ref: a commit or a ref of RECORDS_REPO that holds every file KIT-MANIFEST names (each is checked
# against its KIT-MANIFEST sha256, whatever commit it came from)
RECORDS_REF=<the internal records ref>
# the release scanner of record (the shipped-tree scan of the drivers step), in its own directory beside its
# SHA256SUMS; regen.sh pins that SHA256SUMS by sha256
SCANNER=<path of the release scanner of record>
# the worker roster: a TSV whose column 1 is a worker name (the shipped-tree scan's control; the kit's name scan)
ROSTER=<path of the worker roster TSV>
#
# Read by the kit (its env.sh template refuses each one unset):
# the cgif donor clone (cgif/cgif_file_fuzzer at the donors' released lib), with cgif's four pinned images untracked in
# its projects/cgif/bin/cgif_file_fuzzer/
DON=<the cgif donor clone>
# the start-up collector's build helpers (read-only)
S=<the start-up collector's helper directory>
# the month the notices of record name, YYYY-MM
TRANSB_MONTH=<YYYY-MM>
# the ASan kit's tools directory (the ELF map tool, the remap tool, the ELF reader)
KIT=<the ASan kit's tools directory>
# the cgif donor's build workspace name on VM
DWS=<the donor's build workspace name>
# the proofs repository checkout every stage reads commits from
TRANSB_OVPI=<a checkout of the proofs repository>
# cgif's released symbol cache of the address checker (the port_core base of YF0m)
TRANSB_OLDSYMS=<path of cgif's symbol cache>
# libreac/fuzz_decode's pinned image B and its unstripped twin (the controls of the generators)
TRANSB_DECB=<path of fuzz_decode.asan-ubsan>
TRANSB_DECBS=<path of fuzz_decode.asan-ubsan, unstripped>
# libreac/fuzz_grant's pinned image B and its unstripped twin (the controls of the generators)
TRANSB_GRB=<path of fuzz_grant.asan-ubsan>
TRANSB_GRBS=<path of fuzz_grant.asan-ubsan, unstripped>
# the address checker's cache directory
TRANSB_PACCACHE=<the address checker's cache directory>
# the donor binaries the address checker reads
TRANSB_DONORBIN=<the donor binaries directory>
# the directory that holds the binary-match scripts (read by exitdrv)
TRANSB_BINMATCH=<the binary-match scripts directory>
# the pinned-build root of libreac
TRANSB_LROOT=<the pinned-build root of libreac>
# the address checker of record, in its versioned directory (the other versions sit beside it)
TRANSB_PACEFA1=<the address checker's versioned directory>
# reac-repacer's pinned-build root (fuzz_uci image B, exitdrv's role-identity reference; fuzz_lock B, the gates' known answers)
TRANSB_REFROOT=<the pinned-build root of reac-repacer>
# the integrator's premise draft of this unit (read-only; acej's list cross-check)
TRANSB_DRAFT=<path of the premise draft>
# image A's AF0m.v for THESE pins: <commit>:<path> in TRANSB_OVPI (the image-A row's committed lib/A)
TRANSB_PAIRA_FROM=<commit>:proofs/<project>/<unit>/lib/A/AF0m.v
# the cold-start build launcher (cb)
TRANSB_CBTOOL=<path of the build launcher>
# the build-VM ssh / scp wrapper (the collector's VM steps)
TRANSB_OSSVVM=<path of the build-VM wrapper>
# the build-VM workspace that holds the unit's compiled statements
TRANSB_STMTWS=<the statements workspace name>
# the worker table: column 1 = every worker name (the kit's name scan)
TRANSB_WORKERS_TSV=<path of the worker table>
# the build VMs' cold-build root, expanded by the VM's shell
TRANSB_VMOB=<the build VMs' cold-build root>
# the cold bases table (unit, base commit, facts commit, utc): the pin authority and the build base
TRANSB_BASETSV=<path of the cold bases table>
# the build check's scratch clone name (cb clone at the unit's current base; never pushed)
TRANSB_BUILD_CLONE=<the build check's clone name>
